["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/securityThreatModel", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Ne71d607080c343f6b208e82e2856946a", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/availableFrom", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
